<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pierre-Paul de La Grandière</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1807–1876</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pierre-Paul de La Grandière was a French admiral and governor of Cochinchina from 1863 to 1868. He organised the administration of the three eastern provinces ceded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862">Treaty of Saigon</a> in 1862, brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> under French protection in 1863, and in 1867 seized the three western provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> delta, completing the colony of French Cochinchina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pierre-paul-de-la-grandiere.jpg" alt="Pierre-Paul de La Grandière" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: G.Garitan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:De_la_Grandi%C3%A8re_amiral_05097.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
